forti-api (1.3.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Add fortiapi::system::feed_status() and FeedStatus: a threat feed's loaded
    state, error, file status, accepted/valid/invalid counts, device-wide entry
    cap (limit), overflow flag and last content update, from one entry-list
    request that transfers no entries (start past the end, count=1: FortiOS
    counts valid/invalid only up to the end of the window).
  * Add fortiapi::system::feed_entries(feed, start, count): one server-side
    page of a feed's entries; count 0 sends no request.
  * feed_state shares the reply parsing; entry validity sent as text is read
    too.
  * Live suite: FORTI_API_LIVE_NO_PURGE=1 skips the leftover purge; new live
    test for feed status counts and paging.

