forti-api (1.2.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Add fortiapi::ChildTable<Spec, &Type::attribute> (Table<Spec>::child<...>):
    list, find, get, contains, add, update and del of single entries of a table
    attribute on cmdb child paths (cmdb/<path>/<parent key>/<attribute>[/<entry
    key>]); updates send only the entry's changes.
  * Generated table entry structs and fortiapi::Ref name their key member
    (static constexpr mkey); `mkey` is now a reserved member name in the
    generator.
  * Reply records child_path, child_mkey, http_method, old_revision and
    revision_changed. On child paths mkey is the new entry's key on POST, the
    parent's on PUT and the entry's on DELETE (FortiOS 7.4.8, validated live);
    ChildTable::add takes a device-assigned key from child_mkey or from mkey of
    a child POST reply.
  * Live suite: the guard admits writes on child paths of forti-api-test-*
    objects in approved collections (name-keyed entries must be
    forti-api-test-* too); new live tests for address-group members,
    access-list rules, the config-log attribution of child writes and
    concurrent writers.
  * fortiapi::schema: child_table(), child_path() and created_entry_key(), the
    runtime counterparts of ChildTable's attribute check, paths and
    device-assigned key; ChildTable::add and created_entry_key share one rule
    (detail::created_entry_key, detail::reported_number). Unit tests compare
    child_path with ChildTable::path (id- and name-keyed, dot keys) and
    created_entry_key with add() on the 7.4.8 reply shapes.

 -- Cooper Larson <cooper@valkyrianlabs.com>  Sat, 17 Oct 2026 17:56:50 +0000

forti-api (1.1.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Recommend valkyrianlabs-archive-keyring so renewed APT signing-key metadata
    reaches existing installs through upgrades (it owns
    /usr/share/keyrings/valkyrianlabs.gpg and links an unmodified
    /etc/apt/keyrings/valkyrianlabs.gpg to it).
  * Portable number parsing: floating-point values sent as text no longer use
    std::from_chars (missing from Apple libc++ before Xcode 26, which broke
    every build on macOS 15); integers unchanged.
  * The runtime schema tables have hidden visibility (#pragma GCC visibility),
    so consumers' executables no longer resolve thousands of weak symbols at
    start-up (forti-cli: 25 ms to 5 ms).

