forti-api (1.0.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Add Client::download and Monitor::download: raw (non-JSON) reply bodies,
    text or binary, through the client's transport, authentication, TLS,
    timeouts, retry policy and ApiError mapping.
    - DownloadOptions: max_bytes (default 64 MiB; SizeLimitError, partial data
      wiped, never retried) and an optional chunked sink; Download carries
      status, Content-Type, Content-Disposition, body and byte count.
    - on_exchange records of successful downloads omit the body.
    - Transport extension, source-compatible: defaulted HttpRequest::max_body /
      on_body and HttpResponse::headers (with case-insensitive header());
      CurlTransport captures headers and enforces both through
      detail::BodyWriter.
  * Live suite: read-only configuration backup test (memory only) and
    FORTI_API_LIVE_READ_ONLY=1, which refuses every write and skips the
    leftover purge.
  * Writes are never sent twice: CurlTransport gives every POST/PUT/DELETE a
    new connection (CURLOPT_FRESH_CONNECT, CURLOPT_FORBID_REUSE), HTTP/1.1 and
    no Expect: 100-continue, so libcurl's internal re-send of a request that
    got nothing back on a reused keep-alive connection (Curl_retry_request) can
    no longer repeat a write that reached the device. A dropped write reply is
    a TransportError with before_send() false. Costs one TCP+TLS handshake per
    write; reads keep the shared connection.
  * fortiapi::path() sends a key that is exactly "." or ".." as %2E / %2E%2E,
    and CurlTransport sets CURLOPT_PATH_AS_IS, so such keys can no longer
    address the table or its parent.
  * Config::max_reply_depth (default 256): a 2xx JSON reply nested deeper is a
    DecodeError, checked while parsing (nlohmann parser callback); a too-deep
    error reply is kept as {"raw": body}.
  * As a Meson subproject, forti-api builds no example or tests and installs no
    headers or .pc; standalone builds are unchanged.

 -- Cooper Larson <cooper@valkyrianlabs.com>  Thu, 15 Oct 2026 13:53:38 +0000

forti-api (1.0.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Generate every cmdb endpoint from FortiOS 7.4.8 schema snapshots (487 on a
    FortiGate-60F) and typed read-only monitor endpoints from sanitized GUI
    recon shapes (tools/fortios, codegen/).
  * Add fortiapi::Field<T> (absent/populated/modified/cleared; updates send
    only changes), Table<Spec>, Singleton<Spec>, MonitorGet<Spec>, per-group
    headers and an endpoint registry.
  * Replace the transport with fortiapi::Client: timeouts, keep-alive,
    percent-encoded keys, Query builder, typed errors, no retries of mutations
    after a possible send, gzip only (FortiOS log replies are deflate streams
    libcurl cannot decode).
  * Remove the pre-generation API (FortiAPI, FortiAuth, FortiGate::/System::
    accessors, types/**); port DNS category, threat feed, schedule, service and
    trusthost helpers to generated types.
  * Decode unset integers reported as "" as absent and numbers sent as text.
  * Ship a source archive and a Homebrew formula (valkyrianlabs/homebrew-tap);
    publish the docs.
  * Tests: network-free unit suite (CI, ASan/UBSan); opt-in live suite behind a
    guard transport and a config-change-log audit, with decode coverage of
    every endpoint and CRUD round-trips on 24 approved inert collections.

